{% comment %}
  ============================================================================
  Homepage — "New Product" PDF callout (top of page)
  ============================================================================
  One-off request, unrelated to the Community page work — DXB asked to replace the section at
  the very top of templates/index.json (`section_VDmBDL`, DXB's own "newproductcallout"), which
  had been hand-assembled via the theme editor per task 0003/Task 11's guidance-only howto as a
  deeply nested native Group > Group > Button structure with a separate Text block. DXB called
  the result "very poor" and asked for a real rebuild, replacing it with a lean bfbella-* custom
  section instead — the same "narrow, low-bloat" approach already used for the Community page's
  social-links section, which DXB specifically liked and asked to see applied here too.

  PRODUCTION REFERENCE: fetched buyflorabella.com directly (confirmed still serving the old
  Hydrogen/Oxygen app in production — 52 `oxygen-v2` asset references, not this Shopify theme —
  but the actual design intent is real, current content, not stale mockup data). The real markup
  is a single flex-wrap row of two pill buttons (hot pink fill, lime border + ring-offset glow,
  bold uppercase, hover scale+darken) followed by one italic caption line with "amazing" in
  bold. This section reproduces that closely, with every color resolved through the theme's own
  palette (never hardcoded) so DXB can dial in the exact production hex via the native color
  picker if `color5`/`color8` aren't close enough on their own.

  BLOCKS, not fixed fields: production's 2 buttons are tied to whatever products are being
  promoted "this month" — genuinely rotating content, not a fixed evergreen CTA pair (unlike
  e.g. bfbella-about-cta.liquid's fixed 2 buttons). Built as a block repeater
  (bfbella-callout-button) so DXB can add/remove/reorder promo links over time without needing
  new section fields each time.

  MESSAGE: richtext field (same reasoning as bfbella-about-story.liquid's Mission paragraphs
  update) so "amazing" (or whatever word matters that month) can be bolded via the native
  toolbar — matches production's `<span class="font-bold">amazing</span>` inside an otherwise
  italic line.

  CONTENT: real production copy and PDF links carried over directly from the section being
  replaced (same URLs, confirmed unchanged) — see templates/index.json for where they're set.

  DEPLOY: written directly into this live repo's working tree as part of the 2026-09-07
  live-edit pilot (see claude_docs/build_docs/live_edit_pilot_plan.md) — DXB reviews, then
  commits and pushes by hand.
  ============================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign bg = section.settings.background_color | default: settings.color_palette.background

  if section.settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id, skip_contrast: true
  endif
%}

<div
  id="NewProductCallout-{{ section.id }}"
  class="bfbella-new-product-callout{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
  style="
    --bfbella-bg: {{ bg }};
    {% if section.settings.padding_top != blank %}--bfbella-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;{% endif %}
    {% if section.settings.padding_bottom != blank %}--bfbella-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;{% endif %}
  "
>
  <div class="bfbella-new-product-callout__inner page-width">

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="bfbella-new-product-callout__buttons">
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.message != blank -%}
      <div class="bfbella-new-product-callout__message">{{ section.settings.message }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .bfbella-new-product-callout {
    padding-block-start: var(--bfbella-pad-top, 5rem);
    padding-block-end: var(--bfbella-pad-bottom, 2rem);
    background-color: var(--bfbella-bg);
  }

  .bfbella-new-product-callout__inner {
    max-width: 80rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-new-product-callout__buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-new-product-callout__message {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-foreground);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .bfbella-new-product-callout__message strong {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "BFBella — New Products",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-wrapper",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "bfbella-callout-button"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "message",
      "label": "Caption message",
      "info": "Rendered italic. Use the toolbar to bold specific words."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "Background color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the theme's base background. Production uses a warm off-white (#F5F5F0) — pick that exact shade here if you want a precise match, or leave blank for the theme's plain background."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 32
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "BFBella — New Products",
      "category": "Custom",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "bfbella-callout-button" },
        { "type": "bfbella-callout-button" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
